ds `landed = [*attached, *referencing]` (where `attached = _attached_commit_shas(...)`), and the existence check raises at line 215-216 on `if own_impact and not landed:`. Attached SHAs are already unioned into the existence check.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fad9ba79dc172d866","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Root cause section; close_precheck.py lines 182-183, 215-223","norm_id":"nd94fa6325b813ef0","priority":0.9,"reason":"high-priority+criterion-opted-in","recalled":false,"scenarios":["The reported reproduction would already succeed on the shipped tree, since an attached SHA populates `landed` and suppresses the raise at line 215."],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":0.9,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"no","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"no","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"yes","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"module","debt_impact":"medium","divergent_implementation":"contradicts_reality","dod_uncertifiable":"certification_cannot_prove","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"high","prod_impact":"medium","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.75,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Correct the call-site count for _attached_commit_shas: it is called at line 182 (existence check) and line 316 (diff check), not 'exactly ONE call site at ~line 327'.","cohort":["E4"],"criteria":["E4"],"decision":"block","decision_margin":0.15,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan: '_attached_commit_shas ... has exactly ONE call site, ~line 327, inside _check_file_impact_vs_diff. That function runs only AFTER line 226 has already raised.'","Code: call at line 182 (`attached = _attached_commit_shas(...)` in _check_work_landed); call at line 316 (`attached = _attached_commit_shas(...)` in _check_file_impact_vs_diff); line 327 is `raise CommandError(` inside the diff loop."],"finding":"The plan asserts '_attached_commit_shas ... has exactly ONE call site, ~line 327, inside _check_file_impact_vs_diff.' This is false in the shipped code: _attached_commit_shas is called at line 182 (inside _check_work_landed, feeding the existence check) AND at line 316 (inside _check_file_impact_vs_diff). Line 327 is a `raise CommandError`, not a call site.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f83fb7a0219e520e3","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Root cause section; close_precheck.py lines 182, 316, 327","norm_id":"n53618444f3fe491c","priority":0.9,"reason":"high-priority+criterion-opted-in","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Any reader relying on the 'exactly ONE call site' claim to reason about the fix would be misled."],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":0.9,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"no","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"no","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"yes","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"module","debt_impact":"medium","divergent_implementation":"contradicts_reality","dod_uncertifiable":"certification_cannot_prove","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"high","prod_impact":"medium","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.75,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Verify against the shipped tree that the claimed existence/diff union asymmetry exists; the code unions both (line 183/215 and line 318), so re-ground the 'asymmetry is the bug' claim or withdraw it.","cohort":["E4"],"criteria":["E4"],"decision":"block","decision_margin":0.15,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan: 'the two commit sources are unioned for the DIFF check and are not unioned for the EXISTENCE check. The asymmetry is the bug.'","Code: existence check uses `landed = [*attached, *referencing]` (line 183, re-computed line 214) at the raise on line 215; diff check unions `attached + list(referencing)` at line 318. Both are unioned."],"finding":"The plan claims the two commit sources 'are not unioned for the EXISTENCE check' and 'The asymmetry is the bug.' The shipped code unions them for BOTH checks (line 182 for existence via `landed`, line 316 for diff), so there is no asymmetry to be the bug.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f58ba85730fbf8f49","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Root cause section; close_precheck.py lines 182-183/214-215 vs 316","norm_id":"n449234fde7d2e31a","priority":0.9,"reason":"high-priority+criterion-opted-in","recalled":false,"scenarios":["The regression oracle in AC-2 ('that test FAILS if the union at the existence check is reverted to the scan alone') cannot be constructed against a union that is already the shipped mechanism and whose removal is not what the plan patches."],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":0.9,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"no","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"no","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_clai